WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.890
What is one-half of 4 counters? Let us think carefully. Share 4 into 2 equal groups

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:08.115
to get 2 in each. The answer is 2. Great work!

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:13.767
What is one-third of 6 counters? Let us think carefully. Share 6 into 3 equal groups

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:17.078
to get 2 in each. The answer is 2. Great work!

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:22.560
What is one-quarter of 8 counters? Let us think carefully. Share 8 into 4 equal

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:26.249
groups to get 2 in each. The answer is 2. Great work!

00:00:27.117 --> 00:00:31.632
What is one-fifth of 10 counters? Let us think carefully. Share 10 into 5 equal

00:00:31.632 --> 00:00:35.245
groups to get 2 in each. The answer is 2. Great work!
